                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Over the last decade, 85% of new medicines entered the American market. Meanwhile, countries like Canada fell further behind by admitting less than half of new medicines available. Canadians were then forced to seek treatment in the U.S.\n\nThe Biden admin.\u2019s current price control scheme puts the U.S. in lockstep with countries like Canada, and it will ultimately risk patients\u2019 access to innovative and cutting-edge medicines.",
